WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.689
Movies can be the perfect way for couples
to pass the time.

00:00:03.689 --> 00:00:08.640
They're entertaining, easily shared experiences,
and they tend to teach us a thing or two about

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.940
each other's tastes.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.390
There are some movies, however, that are probably
best viewed alone so as to avoid arguments,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.030
general awkwardness, or sudden distrust.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.380
These films are totally worth your time…as
long as you're by yourself.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:26.199
Fair warning: There are spoilers aplenty about
each of these titles.

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:27.770
Gone Girl

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.870
David Fincher's adaptation of the creepy mystery
novel Gone Girl is the kind of movie that

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.569
can easily leave partners second-guessing
what they really know about one another.

00:00:37.569 --> 00:00:42.309
Chances are, your lover isn't going to disappear
and frame you for it just out of spite.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:46.790
But given the graphic lengths to which Rosamund
Pike's "Amazing Amy" was willing to go to

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:51.690
deliver payback to Ben Affleck's cheating
Nick Dunne, it's just better to avoid the

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.649
potential for romantic fallout that might
result from sharing a viewing.

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:59.679
That said, it's still totally worth a solo
screening because it's still a pretty solid

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:03.260
adaptation of an intensely gripping narrative.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.879
Sweet November

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:09.920
For a movie that's been billed as a romantic
drama, Sweet November sure has its twistier

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:10.920
moments.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.520
The film centers around Charlize Theron's
character Sara Deever who, at first, seems

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.899
like your prototypical precocious manic pixie
dream girl.

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:25.710
But as Keanu Reeves' Nelson Moss, soon discovers,
she has a devastating secret beneath all those

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:26.710
scarves.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.229
For some, this might seem like a heart-wrenching
story of star-crossed love, but for others,

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:35.470
it might just be maddening that this poor
schmuck could be duped into giving his heart

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.290
to someone so tragic.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.570
In the interest of avoiding unnecessary arguments
on the homefront, this one's best reserved

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.580
for a solo screening.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.070
Unfaithful

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:49.350
Any attempt at discussing this movie is going
to start an argument, guaranteed.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.439
Diane Lane's character Connie Summer is a
married mother in a lustless marriage, but

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:59.679
that all changes when she comes across Olivier
Martinez's character Paul Martel.

00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:04.890
The resulting affair is sensuous and intoxicating,
but has grave consequences for her marriage

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.180
and her paramour.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.830
Without spoiling all of the details, let's
just say that crimes of the heart aren't the

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.240
only ones that result from her duplicity.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.990
It's what happens next that's bound to be
a point of severe derision from those who

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.410
regard adultery to be the ultimate deal-breaker.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:23.730
So, to avoid the conversation catastrophe
that's sure to ensue from watching this movie

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:27.470
on date night, save it for a rainy day all
by your lonesome.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.810
The Good Girl

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.830
Jennifer Aniston fans will definitely want
to see this movie because The Good Girl marks

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.940
an impressive departure from the generic rom-com
fare she's usually found in.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.920
That said, this one is also completely Not
Safe for Couples.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.870
The movie revolves around her store clerk
character Justine being stuck in an emotionless

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:51.840
marriage, until she's swept up by her handsome,
albeit obsessive coworker, played by Jake

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:52.900
Gyllenhaal.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.690
From there, things seem to spiral out of control
for all characters involved, and let's just

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.480
say the potential for post-credits squabbling
looms large.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.840
So it's best to just steer clear of coupling
up for this cinematic experience altogether.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.180
Revolutionary Road

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:14.030
Kate Winslet and Leonardo DiCaprio made blockbuster
magic together in Titanic—and their reunion

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.320
a decade later for Revolutionary Road was
nothing to shake a stick at either.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.230
The two play the Wheelers, a couple who share
two kids and a run-of-the-mill '50s suburbanite

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.810
existence but grow increasingly unhappy with
each other and their place in the world.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:31.610
They eventually decide to move to France,
where she can be the breadwinner—but when

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.360
she becomes pregnant with their third child,
everything falls apart in a spectacular series

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.890
of screen arguments that showcase the actors'
gifts for cutting remarks.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:45.640
At the same time, the movie's unblinking look
at the demise of a once-perfect couple can

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:50.310
easily plant the seeds of doubt into even
the most promising pair, so don't go queueing

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.000
this one up on date night.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.880
Away from Her

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.570
Sarah Polley's adaptation of the Alice Munro
short story "The Bear Came Over the Mountain"

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:03.040
is a masterclass in film making in many ways,
but it isn't likely to give couples a case

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.210
of good vibrations.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:09.580
A man who deeply loves his wife watches as
her Alzheimer's washes away all memory of

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.350
the life they shared, while she gives her
heart to a fellow patient who suffers from

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.680
a similar condition.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:19.130
Naturally, he tries to break them up by running
interference, but he eventually finds that

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.010
his wife's broken heart outweighs his own.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:26.470
Needless to say, it's heartbreaking—and
for any couple hoping they'll grow old together,

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:31.130
this might be a rude wake-up call that invites
all kinds of ethical debates.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.370
The Gift

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:38.130
With The Gift, Joel Edgerton proved his talents
extend well beyond a strong screen presence.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:43.120
The accomplished actor made his writer-director
debut with this eerie mystery-thriller, and

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:48.660
pulled off one of the most satisfying—and
unsettlingly ambiguous—endings in the entire

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.660
genre.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:55.090
As Gordo, a man who shares a mysterious past
with Jason Bateman's character, Edgerton lingers

00:04:55.090 --> 00:05:00.350
at the margins of everything his old acquaintance
has built for himself—a great job, a beautiful

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.870
wife and home, and even a growing family.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:07.260
The title "gift" can be seen in several different
ways during the movie, but perhaps the movie's

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:11.100
most lasting effect is the gnawing sensation
it leaves you with.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.590
Questions like "Who was right?," are bound
to pop up after letting this mindtrip of a

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.590
movie sink in.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.010
So, definitely check it out … just wait
'til your significant other is otherwise occupied

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.350
before pressing play.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.590
Thanks for watching!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.320
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

